; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   100   \DESCRIPTION    Function call with pointer to element of deque dynamic data. Precondition assures that a valid
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   101                   deque pointer is provided to this function.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   102   \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_DEQUE_DYN_M]
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   103  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   104  \ID SBSW_OS_AWA_DEQUE_BUFFER
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   105   \DESCRIPTION    Array write access to data buffer of deque. Precondition assures that a valid deque pointer is provided
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   106                   to this function. Review has shown that the read/write index of the deque dynamic data is initialized
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   107                   to zero and afterwards only changed by functions Os_DequeIdxIncrement, Os_DequeIdxDecrement and
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   108                   Os_DequeDelete which guarantee that the index is kept in valid range.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   109   \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_DEQUE_DYN_M]
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   110                   \M [CM_OS_DEQUE_BUFFER_SIZE_M]
