; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   113   \DESCRIPTION    Array write access to data buffer of deque. Precondition assures that a valid deque pointer is provided
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   114                   to this function. Review has shown that the local read/write index is initialized from a valid index
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   115                   and afterwards only changed by function Os_DequeIdxIncrement which performs a check against the
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   116                   configured size in order to keep the index in valid range.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   117   \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_DEQUE_DYN_M]
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Deque.c	   118                   \M [CM_OS_DEQUE_BUFFER_SIZE_M]
